      "When they pulled up outside the address at the end of the quiet cul-de-sac, the mood shifted. The house was strikingly symmetrical. Every shrub looked trimmed with nail scissors; every curtain hung at an identical, breathless angle. It looked less like a home where people lived, and more like an architectural render that had forgotten to install human warmth.",
