      "Three weeks evaporated in a blur of fabric swatches, phone calls, and Wardah furiously cooking batches of sweets to freeze for guests. Abdul managed the logistics with the brisk efficiency of a hotel grand opening, while Ma’un walked around the house like a ghost who had forgotten how to haunt.",
      "Then, the ninth of November arrived not with trumpet blasts, but with the quiet scrape of luggage against tile.",
      "In her bedroom—the room she had slept in for nineteen years—Naba packed her belongings into a single medium-sized bag. The room looked untouched. No posters on the pale walls. No personal knick-knacks cluttering the dresser. The bed was made so tightly that a coin could bounce on the sheets. She had lived in this house for nearly two decades, yet she had left behind zero footprints, as though terrified that leaving a trace of herself would be considered an imposition.",
      "A small shadow fell across the threshold.",
      "Sara stood in the doorway, clutching a soft embroidered handkerchief, her knuckles white. She didn’t look at the bag. She looked at Naba’s shoes.",
      "“You’re really leaving?” the little girl asked. Her voice was thin, trying very hard not to wobble.",
      "Naba knelt down on the cold floor, bringing herself to eye level. She reached out and smoothed the collar of Sara’s dress, then tucked a stray strand of hair behind her little sister’s ear—a quiet, gentle habit she had performed every morning before school.",
